hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22691","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Hammam al-Sha'bani, who said: A man of Khath'am narrated to me, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the expedition of Tabuk, so he stood one night and his companions gathered to him, and said: Allah gave me tonight the two treasures, the treasure of Persia and Rome, and aided me with kings, the kings of Himyar, except the two red ones; and there is no dominion but to Allah. They come taking from the wealth of Allah and fighting in the path of Allah. He said it three times."
